' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Full Zachman 6x6 with every cell holding a representative artifact/primitive.
'   usecase:      Teach the complete primitive models per cell.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       enterprise / classification-taxonomy
' ============================================================================
title Example Zachman - Complex Full 6x6 (all cells)

note as TopNote
  All 36 cells populated with their primitive model type.
  Each cell is a primitive (single-interrogative) model.
  Composite models combine cells; Zachman keeps them separate on purpose.
  Grid via nested packages (row -> column cell).
end note

package "Planner row" as PR {
  rectangle "P-What: List of Things" as P1
  rectangle "P-How: List of Processes" as P2
  rectangle "P-Where: Locations" as P3
  rectangle "P-Who: Org Units" as P4
  rectangle "P-When: Event List" as P5
  rectangle "P-Why: Vision/Goals" as P6
}

package "Owner row" as OR {
  rectangle "O-What: Semantic Model" as O1
  rectangle "O-How: Business Process" as O2
  rectangle "O-Where: Logistics Net" as O3
  rectangle "O-Who: Work Flow" as O4
  rectangle "O-When: Master Schedule" as O5
  rectangle "O-Why: Business Plan" as O6
}

package "Designer row" as DR {
  rectangle "D-What: Logical Data Model" as D1
  rectangle "D-How: System Function Model" as D2
  rectangle "D-Where: System Geography" as D3
  rectangle "D-Who: Human Interface Arch" as D4
  rectangle "D-When: Event/Time Model" as D5
  rectangle "D-Why: Business Rule Model" as D6
}

package "Builder row" as BR {
  rectangle "B-What: Physical Data Model" as B1
  rectangle "B-How: Program Spec" as B2
  rectangle "B-Where: Network Architecture" as B3
  rectangle "B-Who: Role/Task Model" as B4
  rectangle "B-When: Control Structure" as B5
  rectangle "B-Why: Rule Specification" as B6
}

package "Programmer row" as PGR {
  rectangle "Pg-What: Data Definition" as Pg1
  rectangle "Pg-How: Source Code" as Pg2
  rectangle "Pg-Where: Network Config" as Pg3
  rectangle "Pg-Who: User Screen" as Pg4
  rectangle "Pg-When: Job Schedule" as Pg5
  rectangle "Pg-Why: Rule Implementation" as Pg6
}

package "User row" as UR {
  rectangle "U-What: Usable Data" as U1
  rectangle "U-How: Executable Function" as U2
  rectangle "U-Where: Usable Network" as U3
  rectangle "U-Who: User Role" as U4
  rectangle "U-When: Trigger Event" as U5
  rectangle "U-Why: Enforced Strategy" as U6
}

' Refinement chains down key columns.
P1 --> O1 --> D1 --> B1 --> Pg1 --> U1 : refines (What column)
P2 --> O2 --> D2 --> B2 --> Pg2 --> U2 : refines (How column)
P3 --> O3 --> D3 --> B3 --> Pg3 --> U3 : refines (Where column)
